# .last-agent — integrity checkpoint for the next AI coding agent

**Agent:** LongCat — 2026-10-07 (Phase 2 implementation)
**Branch:** fix/upgrade-removal-safety
**Last commit (base):** see `git log -1`

## Summary

Implemented Phase 2 of the upgrade-removal-safety plan: the conflict-logic fix in
`gems/arch/updates.py`.

**The fix:** `_map_conflicts` now distinguishes between one-provider and many-provider
virtual name conflicts:
- **One provider** (typically the real package being superseded) — expansion is correct
  and preserved (e.g., `7zip` provides `p7zip`, conflicts `p7zip` → removing `p7zip` is CORRECT).
- **Many providers** (a virtual role name like `ADIOS-MODULE`, `NVIDIA-MODULE`,
  `vulkan-driver`) — expansion is wrong. The declaration means "only one may fill this
  role," not "delete the twelve others." Atlas no longer pre-emptively removes; pacman
  resolves this during the transaction.

**Also fixed:** `_add_to_remove` used `set.update(pname)` which added the *characters* of
a package name, not the name itself. Changed to `set.add(pname)`.

**Tests added (5):**
- `test__no_removal_when_conflict_on_virtual_name_with_many_providers` — the adios-dkms incident shape
- `test__still_removes_when_conflict_on_virtual_name_with_one_provider` — one-provider expansion preserved
- `test__still_removes_real_package_conflict` — real package conflicts still work
- `test__no_removal_when_many_kernels_provide_same_virtual_name` — 17 kernels, no removals
- `test__add_to_remove_records_whole_package_names` — the set.add fix

**Verification:** 867 Python tests pass (was 822 on master + 5 new + Phase 1 tests).
JS contract tests green. No regressions.

## Known gaps / next steps

- **NOT GUI-verified.** The failure mode is a removed kernel, so verification belongs in a
  disposable Arch/CachyOS container, never on a real machine. Manual pass: run Update All
  against a system with multiple kernel variants; no removal should be proposed.
- **Phase 1 + Phase 2 are both on this branch** — the branch now has 13 commits ahead of
  master. Needs a rebase + PR + merge.
- **The stale-database / reinstall-instead-of-upgrade bug** (found 2026-09-09) is still
  not planned — separate issue.
- **Observability gap:** Atlas does not log what the providers dialog offered or what the
  user selected. For a choice that can cascade into deleting the running kernel, that is a
  serious gap. Closing it is a prerequisite for trusting Phase 2 in the wild.
